{"name":"Groundcover","hex":"#64634d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"groundcover","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of ground cover."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/groundcover"}],"entries":[{"title":"Groundcover","blocks":[{"text":"Groundcover or ground cover is any plant that grows low over an area of ground, which protects the topsoil from erosion and drought. In a terrestrial ecosystem, the ground cover forms the layer of vegetation below the shrub layer known as the herbaceous layer, and provides habitats and concealments for terrestrial fauna. The most widespread ground covers are grasses of various types."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Vinca_major1.jpg/330px-Vinca_major1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Groundcover","wikidata":"Q889491"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/D%C3%BClmen%2C_G%C3%B6versheide_--_2015_--_7718-22.jpg/500px-D%C3%BClmen%2C_G%C3%B6versheide_--_2015_--_7718-22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/D%C3%BClmen%2C_G%C3%B6versheide_--_2015_--_7718-22.jpg/1280px-D%C3%BClmen%2C_G%C3%B6versheide_--_2015_--_7718-22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/D%C3%BClmen%2C_G%C3%B6versheide_--_2015_--_7718-22.jpg/500px-D%C3%BClmen%2C_G%C3%B6versheide_--_2015_--_7718-22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Groundcover in a forest in Dülmen, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AD%C3%BClmen%2C_G%C3%B6versheide_--_2015_--_7718-22.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Microstegium_vimineum.JPG/500px-Microstegium